  "policy": {
   "nbp_reference": 3.75,
   "next_mpc_label": "MPC next: 8-9 Apr",
   "pricing_text": "FRAs at the 9 Mar close (1x4 3.81, 3x6 3.82, 6x9 3.82, 9x12 3.92 vs WIBOR 3M 3.79) price roughly 15bp of NBP hikes within 12 months. The MPC cut by 25bp to 3.75% on 4 Mar (a 'hawkish cut', ING); the projection excludes the war. Glapiński (5 Mar): if things calm within about two months, one more cut is back on the table; no forward guidance. Wnorowski (6 Mar): no further cuts while the war lasts; Kotecki: room 'much smaller'.",
   "risk_text": "Oil and the war set the direction: if Brent stays near $100 the market keeps pricing NBP hikes and the front-end roll-down reverses; a ceasefire would bring cuts back (Glapiński's 'two months'). SAFE politics add a fiscal premium."
  },
  "macro": {
   "cpi": {
    "v": 2.2,
    "m": "Jan flash (GUS, 13 Feb; old weights)"
   },
   "projection_text": "NBP March projection (4 Mar; data to 19 Feb, war excluded): CPI 50% bands 1.6-2.9% (2026), 1.1-3.7% (2027); central path 2.3% / 2.4% / 2.3% (2026-28), GDP 3.9% in 2026 (Inflation Report, 6 Mar).",
   "fiscal_text": "2025 general-government deficit ~7.0% of GDP (MoF figures in Fitch: 7.0% / 6.5% / 6.2% for 2025-27, debt ~70% of GDP by 2027); 2026 deficit cap PLN 271.7bn.",
   "fiscal_risk_text": "2026 needs ~38% (25 Feb) financed; MoF cancelled the 11 Mar switch; budget accounts ~PLN 171.6bn at end-February. Moody's reviews Poland on 20 Mar (A2, negative).",
   "backdrop_text": "The NBP cut to 3.75% on 4 Mar after holding at 4.00% in January and February; January flash CPI 2.2%; 2025 GDP 3.6%, Q4 4.0%. Ratings: Fitch A- negative (affirmed 27 Feb), Moody's A2 negative, S&P A- stable. 9 Mar: POLGBs fell another ~30bp (2Y 4.22%, 5Y 5.17%, 10Y 5.85%) with Brent near $120 at the open; FRAs now price NBP hikes; MoF cancelled the 11 Mar switch auction on market volatility; ING raised its 2026 CPI forecast to 2.5-3.0%. Late on 9 Mar Brent fell below $90 after Trump said the war was 'basically over'; Mojtaba Khamenei was named leader; Hungary's 10Y hit 7.35%."
  },
  "calendar": {
   "plan_text": "MoF March plan (27 Feb): sale auctions on 18 and 25 Mar (PLN 7-13bn each; OK0128, NZ0331, PS0731 (new 5Y fixed), DS1035, NZ0936 (new 10Y POLSTR floater)) and a switch on 11 Mar buying back OK0426, DS0726, PS1026, WZ1126 and OK0127; no T-bills; WZ sales ended in February. February sales were ~PLN 41bn; ~38% of 2026 needs financed. 9 Mar: MoF cancelled the 11 Mar switch because of market volatility.",
   "timing_text": "The Aug 2025-Feb 2026 pattern (auction-day close the cheapest point of the week) comes from a rally regime; in March's sell-off MoF is cutting supply (switch instead of sale, a smaller 25 Mar offer), so remaining dates (18 and 25 Mar) are less of a supply event. Next MPC 8-9 Apr: a hold is expected while the market prices hikes.",
